# Tuning the difficulty

The **Default difficulty** tab sets the skillcheck used when a script does not choose its own values. A script that passes its own value always wins, so these defaults only change checks that leave that value out.

## The two settings that matter most

| Setting | Easy | Normal | Hard |
|---|---|---|---|
| Needle speed | 1 or 2 | 3 | 4 or 5 |
| Zone size | 1 or 2 | 3 | 4 or 5 |

Change one at a time. A fast needle **and** a small zone together is very hard.

## Making it harder without making it frustrating

- **Repetitions:** 2 or 3 hits in a row. One miss fails the whole check.
- **Needle direction:** *Random each time* stops players learning one rhythm.
- **Start position scatter:** higher values make the timing less predictable. 0 means the needle always starts in the same place.
- **Screen position scatter:** moves the ring away from the centre of the screen.
- **Shake the ring:** the ring wobbles. Set how much with **Shake speed** and **Shake distance**.

## Great hits

The gold part of the zone is a **great** hit. Scripts can reward it (for example a bonus item).

- **Great zone size** is a percentage of the success zone.
- 0 turns great hits off.
- 100 makes every hit a great hit.

## Try it before you save

1. Turn on **Test command** (General tab), save and restart.
2. In game, type `/skillcheck` to try the defaults, or `/skillcheck 4 4 2` for speed 4, zone 4, 2 repetitions.
3. Turn **Test command** off again when you are done. Any player can use it while it is on.

## Sounds

The **Sounds** section of the **Appearance** tab sets the volume. To use your own sounds, replace the files in `ui/sfx/skillcheck/` and keep the same file names (`incoming.mp3`, `good.mp3`, `great.mp3`).
